# The global symbols of runtime/build/avant_rt.o (Stage 28 W12).
#
# runtime/build.sh folds the core units (the collector's avant_gc_*.c
# and avant_rt_traps.c) into avant_rt.o and then keeps global only the
# symbols listed here (objcopy --keep-global-symbols): every other
# symbol the units share with each other is made local, so an internal
# function or variable can cross a unit boundary without becoming part
# of the object's surface. This list is the object's surface: the entry
# points and data generated code and the other runtime objects use,
# plus the internal names that were already global before W12 (the
# stackmap split of the collector stage left them global; localizing
# them changes the surface, so it is a later step, see the W12 record).
# A new global entry point is added here on purpose, never by accident.
# One symbol per line, sorted; `nm -g --defined-only` of the object
# must print exactly this set.
avant_alloc
avant_alloc_c
avant_alloc_in_mature
avant_barrier
avant_barrier_at
avant_bump_alloc
avant_checked_add_i64
avant_checked_add_u64
avant_checked_div_i64
avant_checked_div_u64
avant_checked_mul_i64
avant_checked_mul_u64
avant_checked_rem_i64
avant_checked_rem_u64
avant_checked_sub_i64
avant_checked_sub_u64
